From: Project SunUEFI <source-preparation@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: prefer the validated Piano 120 Hz cold-start mode

Factory Android pen-in-range captures use LCD 120 Hz, hand scan 60 Hz and
pen scan 240 Hz. Linux pen frames have also been observed at a 120 Hz
cold start, while the 144 Hz path and live refresh changes remain under
investigation. Prefer that existing mode for the Piano board so the
normal product does not require an ABI-specific replacement panel module.

Identify the board through its root DT compatible. Do not force a panel
vendor or remove modes; BOE and CSOT still use their own timing sequences.
Other NT36532 boards retain their original first-mode preference.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36532.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36532.c
@@ -198,7 +198,20 @@
 {
 	struct nt36532 *ctx = to_nt36532(panel);
 	const struct panel_info *panel_info = ctx->panel_info;
+	unsigned int preferred = 0;
 	unsigned int i;
+
+	/* Piano's validated pen scan uses a 120 Hz cold-start display mode.
+	 * Keep every advertised mode and each panel vendor's own sequence.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,piano")) {
+		for (i = 0; i < panel_info->num_modes; i++) {
+			if (drm_mode_vrefresh(&panel_info->modes[i]) == 120) {
+				preferred = i;
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < panel_info->num_modes; i++) {
 		struct drm_display_mode *mode;
@@ -208,7 +221,7 @@
 			return -ENOMEM;
 
 		mode->type = DRM_MODE_TYPE_DRIVER;
-		if (i == 0)
+		if (i == preferred)
 			mode->type |= DRM_MODE_TYPE_PREFERRED;
 
 		drm_mode_set_name(mode);
